### Create a Recurring Task [POST]

This api is used to create a recurring task.
<br>
Request Body Parameters :
<table class="humanColumnApiDescription markdown formalTheme">
<tr><td colspan="1"><strong>name</strong><td colspan="1"><strong>Type</strong><td colspan="1"><strong>Description</strong></td></tr>
<tr><td style="padding-right: 40px; width: 140px;">domain_name</td><td>string</td> <td> domain of client web panel</td></tr>
<tr><td style="padding-right: 40px; width: 140px;">access_token</td><td>string</td> <td>access token of individual or corporate</td></tr>
<tr><td style="padding-right: 40px; width: 140px;">vendor_id</td><td> String </td><td> vendor_id for individual or corporate </td></tr>
<tr><td style="padding-right: 40px; width: 140px;">is_multiple_tasks</td><td>boolean</td><td> The value is fixed 1</td></tr>
<tr><td style="padding-right: 40px; width: 140px;">isReccuringTask</td><td> string <br/> (Fixed)</td><td>For recurring task is fixed to true</td></tr>
<tr><td style="padding-right: 40px; width: 140px;">cycle_def</td><td> Object </td><td> specifies “0”->Sunday,”1”->Monday,”2”->Tuesday,”3”->Wednesday,“4”->Thursday,”5”->Friday,”6”->Saturday,specify 1 in front of day id on which the task is scheduled</td></tr>
<tr><td style="padding-right: 40px; width: 140px;">cycle</td><td>integer <br/> (Fixed)</td><td>For recurring task is 1</td></tr>
<tr><td style="padding-right: 40px; width: 140px;">start_date</td><td> string </td><td>start date of recurring task</td></tr>
<tr><td style="padding-right: 40px; width: 140px;">startOn</td><td> string</td><td>start date of recurring task</td></tr>
<tr><td style="padding-right: 40px; width: 140px;">end_date</td><td> string </td><td>end date of recurring task</td></tr>
<tr><td style="padding-right: 40px; width: 140px;">timezone</td><td> string </td><td>Timezone difference with UTC in minutes for e.g., For PST:<code>+480</code> (PDT: <code>+420</code>),For MST <code>+420</code> (MDT:<code>+360</code>) for EST: <code>+300</code>(EDT:<code>+240</code>), for AEST: <code>-600</code> (AEDT: <code>-660</code>), for IST: <code>-330</code>, for CST: <code>+360</code> (CDT:<code>+300</code>)</td></tr>
<tr><td style="padding-right: 40px; width: 140px;">has_pickup</td><td> boolean <br/> (Fixed)</td><td>For a Pickup task and delivery task this is fixed to <code>1</code</td></tr>
<tr><td style="padding-right: 40px; width: 140px;">has_delivery</td><td>boolean <br/> (Fixed)</td><td>For a Pickup task and delivery task this is fixed to <code>1</code></td></tr>
<tr><td style="padding-right: 40px; width: 140px;">layout_type</td><td> integer <br/> (Fixed)</td><td>For a Pickup and delivery task this is fixed to <code>0</code></td></tr>
<tr><td style="padding-right: 40px; width: 140px;">auto_assignment</td><td>boolean</td> <td> If this value is <code>1</code> The task will be auto assigned to the members of the specific team mentioned. or if this value is <code>0</code> it will be unassigned task created. </td></tr>
<tr><td style="padding-right: 40px; width: 140px;">team_id</td><td>integer</td> <td>This is the Unique id of every team. You can get it from the dashBoard. More>teams>respective id of the team will displayed.</td></tr>
<tr><td style="padding-right: 40px; width: 140px;">pickups</td><td>json Array</td><td>Array of objects containing address,name,latitude,longitude,time,phone,template_data,template_name,ref_images,email where address defines pickup address,name defines customer name,latitude defines pickup latitude,longitude defines pickup longitude,time defines pickup time,phone defines customer phone,template_data defines an array of object containing label and data where label defines the custom field name and data will be his value,ref_images defines an array of strings containing links of images,email defines the email of the customer </td></tr>
<tr><td style="padding-right: 40px; width: 140px;">deliveries</td><td>json Array</td><td>Array of objects containing address,name,latitude,longitude,time,phone,template_data,template_name,ref_images,has_return_task,is_package_insured,hadVairablePayment,hadFixedPayment where address defines delivery address,name defines customer name,latitude defines delivery latitude,longitude defines delivery longitude,time defines delivery time,phone defines customer phone,template_data defines an array of object containing label and data where label defines the custom field name and data will be his value,ref_images defines an array of strings containing links of images,has_return_task defines whether task is return task or not,is_package_insured defines whether vendor has insured package by paying insurance ,amount or not if value is <code>0</code> then task is not insured and if value is <code>1</code> task is insured </td></tr>
<tr><td style="padding-right: 40px; width: 140px;">insurance_amount</td><td>string</td><td>is fetched from send_payment_for_task api from key name insurance_amount .</td></tr>
<tr><td style="padding-right: 40px; width: 140px;">total_no_of_tasks</td><td>string</td><td> is fetched from send_payment_for_task api from key name total_no_of_tasks</td></tr>
<tr><td style="padding-right: 40px; width: 140px;">total_service_charge</td><td>string </td><td>is fetched from send_payment_for_task api from key name total_service_charge</td></tr>
<tr><td style="padding-right: 40px; width: 140px;">payment_method</td><td>string</td><td> if the value is <code>8</code> the task payment type is cash,if value is <code>2</code> the task payment method is stripe if value is <code>32</code> the payment method is paystack,if value is <code>131072</code> then payment method is PAGA<code>524288</code> the task payment method is end of month billing if value is</td></tr>
<tr><td style="padding-right: 40px; width: 140px;">amount</td><td> string </td><td> amount is fetched from send_payment_for_task from key per_task_cost </td></tr>
</table>
+ Request (application/json)

